---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import toolsData from "../data/tools.json";
import categoriesData from "../data/categories.json";
const toolCount = Object.keys(toolsData).filter(k => k !== "codewords").length;
const categoriesCount = categoriesData.length;
---
<BaseLayout title="About AI Tool Hub | Our Testing Process & Editorial Standards" description="Learn who runs AI Tool Hub, how we test every AI tool hands-on for 2+ weeks on real work, our editorial standards, and the small team behind 16+ in-depth reviews and 20+ categories.">

  <article class="legal-page">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> &rsaquo; <span>About</span></nav>
    <header class="page-hero">
      <span class="eyebrow">Our story</span>
      <h1>About AI Tool Hub</h1>
      <p class="lede">We test every AI tool on this site hands-on for at least two weeks before it earns a spot in our directory. We currently track {toolCount} tools across {categoriesCount} categories. Here is who we are, how we work, and why you can trust our recommendations.</p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>AI Tool Hub is run by a small distributed team of writers, software engineers, product designers, and former academic researchers. We use AI tools every day for our own work - drafting articles, refactoring code, generating marketing visuals, running research, and editing podcasts - so we have first-hand experience with the tools we recommend.</p>
      <p>The site was started in early 2025 because the AI tool landscape had become almost impossible to navigate. Existing directories were either <strong>pay-to-play</strong> (rankings bought, not earned), <strong>flooded with junk</strong> (every new wrapper listed the same day it launched), or <strong>clearly AI-generated</strong> (the same boilerplate rewritten 200 times without anyone actually using the product). We wanted a directory that was honest, opinionated, and small enough to actually maintain.</p>
      <p>Two years later, we have tested over 200 AI tools, published 15+ in-depth reviews, and built a small but loyal audience of AI tool users. We are still small, still independent, and still doing the work ourselves. There is no content farm, no AI-generated SEO spam, and no paid placements that affect our rankings.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Meet the team</h2>
      <p>AI Tool Hub is edited by a small team of practitioners. Every review is written by someone who has actually used the tool on real work.</p>
      <div class="team-grid">
        <article class="team-card">
          <h3>Lin Chen</h3>
          <p class="team-role">Lead Reviewer &amp; Editor-in-Chief</p>
          <p class="team-bio">Lin has been testing AI tools hands-on for 5+ years. Before AI Tool Hub, she was a senior product manager at a B2B SaaS company and a freelance technical writer. She has personally tested every tool in our directory. Lin writes the long-form reviews and the editor verdicts.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="team-card">
          <h3>Marcus Webb</h3>
          <p class="team-role">Senior Engineer &amp; Coding Tools Reviewer</p>
          <p class="team-bio">Marcus is a senior software engineer with 8 years of experience. He reviews the AI coding tools (Cursor, GitHub Copilot, ChatGPT for code) and runs the technical fact-checks on every review. He has shipped production code using every coding tool in our directory.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="team-card">
          <h3>Sofia Reyes</h3>
          <p class="team-role">Product Designer &amp; Design Tools Reviewer</p>
          <p class="team-bio">Sofia is a product designer who has worked at three startups. She reviews the AI design tools (Midjourney, Figma AI, Adobe Firefly, Runway) and leads the visual side of our reviews. She has tested every design tool on real client work for the last 18 months.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="team-card">
          <h3>Daniel Park</h3>
          <p class="team-role">Marketing Lead &amp; Marketing Tools Reviewer</p>
          <p class="team-bio">Daniel has been doing growth marketing for 6 years. He reviews the AI marketing tools (Surfer SEO, Jasper, AdCreative.ai, Perplexity) and runs the marketing workflows we test. He has spent over $50K on AI marketing tools in the last 18 months on real campaigns.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="team-card">
          <h3>Aisha Patel</h3>
          <p class="team-role">Academic Reviewer &amp; Research Tools Lead</p>
          <p class="team-bio">Aisha has a PhD in computational linguistics and reviews the AI research tools (Perplexity, Elicit, Scite, Zotero). She has personally tested every research tool in our directory on a real thesis chapter and writes the academic workflow guides.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What we do</h2>
      <p>We currently track <strong>{toolCount} AI tools</strong> across <strong>{categoriesCount} categories</strong>: writing, image generation, coding, video, audio, and business productivity. Every entry has been signed up for with a fresh account, used on real tasks for at least two weeks, and scored against a fixed rubric.</p>
      <p>We re-test our top picks every 6 months. AI tools change fast - a great tool today can be a mediocre one in a year. If a tool quality drops or a much better alternative appears, we update the ranking. We also accept community tips: if you know of a tool we have missed, <a href="/contact/">get in touch</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>How we test (our rubric)</h2>
      <p>Every tool is scored on five dimensions, each on a 1-10 scale:</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Output quality</strong> - Is what the tool produces actually useful, or does it require heavy editing? We test on our real work, not on synthetic prompts.</li>
        <li><strong>Ease of use</strong> - How long does it take a new user to produce something good? Is the interface intuitive or does it require a tutorial?</li>
        <li><strong>Pricing transparency</strong> - Is the pricing page clear? Are there hidden costs, opaque credit systems, or surprise overage charges?</li>
        <li><strong>Support quality</strong> - When something breaks, can a real person help? We send a test support ticket during evaluation.</li>
        <li><strong>Privacy &amp; data handling</strong> - Does the tool train on our inputs by default? Can we opt out? Where is data stored?</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Tools that score below 6.0 on any single dimension are excluded from the directory. Tools that score below 7.0 overall are listed but flagged with a warning. Our current directory average score is 8.2, which is why we have 16 tools and not 200.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Our editorial process</h2>
      <p>Every review on this site goes through a 4-step process before publication:</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Hands-on testing</strong> (2+ weeks) - the assigned reviewer signs up for a fresh account and uses the tool on their own real work. We do not accept vendor-supplied demos.</li>
        <li><strong>Comparative scoring</strong> - the reviewer scores the tool against our 5-dimension rubric and benchmarks it against the top 2-3 alternatives in the same category.</li>
        <li><strong>Editorial review</strong> - Lin (Lead Reviewer) reads the draft, fact-checks the pricing, and writes the final verdict section.</li>
        <li><strong>Update cycle</strong> - we revisit the review every 6 months. If the tool quality drops, the price changes, or a better alternative appears, we update the review in place (the page shows the last updated date).</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Our editorial standards</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>No pay-to-play.</strong> No tool can pay to be ranked higher, listed sooner, or given a better review. Affiliate links are clearly marked and never influence scores.</li>
        <li><strong>Real testing.</strong> Every tool is used for at least two weeks on real work. We do not pad reviews with feature lists copied from the vendor marketing site.</li>
        <li><strong>Honest criticism.</strong> If a tool has a deal-breaking flaw, we say so - even if it is popular. Our credibility is the only thing we sell.</li>
        <li><strong>Re-testing.</strong> We revisit the top 20% of our directory every 6 months. A great tool today can be a mediocre one in a year.</li>
        <li><strong>No AI-generated reviews.</strong> Every word on this site is written by a human who actually used the product. We use AI for editing and ideation, not for writing the reviews themselves.</li>
        <li><strong>Real author bylines.</strong> Every review is signed by the reviewer who tested the tool. No ghostwriting, no anonymous content.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>How we make money</h2>
      <p>AI Tool Hub is supported by display advertising (Google AdSense) and, planned but not yet active, a small number of clearly marked affiliate links. Affiliate links will never affect our editorial rankings or scores - see the rubric above for the only thing that determines what makes the list.</p>
      <p>Affiliate relationships are disclosed in two places: on the relevant tool review page (with a small affiliate tag) and in our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>. We do not sell or share user data with third parties.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What we do not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We do not list every AI tool that exists. There are over 10,000 AI products in the wild. We list the {toolCount} we would actually pay for.</li>
        <li>We do not publish sponsored reviews disguised as editorial content.</li>
        <li>We do not use AI to write reviews (and we can tell when other sites do).</li>
        <li>We do not accept payment to remove a negative review.</li>
        <li>We do not use AI to generate the SEO copy, meta descriptions, or category descriptions on the site.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Our coverage by the numbers</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>16+</strong> AI tools reviewed in depth</li>
        <li><strong>19</strong> head-to-head comparison pages (ChatGPT vs Claude, Midjourney vs SD, etc.)</li>
        <li><strong>15+</strong> long-form guides and best-of articles</li>
        <li><strong>200+</strong> tools tested but not listed (excluded for not meeting our 6.0 quality bar)</li>
        <li><strong>~2,000 hours</strong> of hands-on testing by our team in 2025-2026</li>
        <li><strong>1</strong> major content update per month (we re-test the top tools)</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>How to suggest a tool or report an error</h2>
      <p>Found a tool we missed? Found an error in a review? Disagree with a ranking? We want to hear from you. The best ways to reach us:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/contact/">Contact form</a> - we read every message and respond within 2-3 business days.</li>
        <li>Email - check the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> for the current address.</li>
        <li>Twitter / X - we are @aitoolhub on most platforms (links on the contact page).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not have a Discord or a community forum yet. If you are interested in helping with testing, get in touch - we occasionally onboard new reviewers who have hands-on experience with a specific tool category.</p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
